{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-kp-4.88-kirby-problem-4.88-eae571f3-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T15:37:58Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-kp-4.88-kirby-problem-4.88-eae571f3-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-kp-4.88-kirby-problem-4.88-eae571f3-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-kp-4.88-kirby-problem-4.88-eae571f3-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/KP-4.88"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Let $\\tau: S^{4} \\to S^{4}$ be a free (hence orientation-reversing) involution. Is there an embedded $S^{2} \\subset S^{4}$ that is invariant under $\\tau$? This is equivalent to the existence of an embedded $\\mathbb{RP}^{2}$ in $S^{4}/\\tau \\cong \\mathbb{RP}^{4}$, carrying the nontrivial class in $H_{2}(\\mathbb{RP}^{4};\\mathbb{Z}/2)$. This condition on the homology class will be assumed for the rest of the problem."}, "statement_sha256": "2d81d24db6bd0825a3fc03cc89cb0e8d9cce2ca19c28fb5ad516aa1e303e9b2e"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-kp-4.88-kirby-problem-4.88-eae571f3-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/KP-4.88"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f571709f7eb5bb066c7e8774bad13f34"}], "problem_contract_sha256": "36963951c0d0f5e950540e3c95bbed